 Typescript Module
===============

```typescript
import { NuxtContent } from '#content'

const metaAI = new NuxtContent('metaAI')
const weTeKBerlin = new NuxtContent('WeTeK Berlin gGmbH')

export default async function generateContent() {
  const about = await metaAI.get('About')
  const disclaimer = await metaAI.get('Disclaimer')
  const artec = await weTeKBerlin.get('WeTeK Berlin gGmbH/Artec')

  const context = await metaAI.get('context')
  const content = await metaAI.get('content')

  const { title, description } = context
  const { research, vision, systemSpokesperson, collaboration, possibilities } = content

  return {
    title: `${title} - ${artec.title}`,
    description,
    research: research.map(item => ({
      ...item,
      content: item.content.replace(/#/g, '##')
    })),
    vision,
    systemSpokesperson,
    collaboration,
    possibilities
  }
}
```

This Typescript module imports the NuxtContent module to fetch data from the content folder. It fetches the necessary data for the metaAI and WeTeK Berlin gGmbH sections, including the About and Disclaimer pages, as well as the Artec program.

The context and content sections are also fetched and destructured to extract the necessary data. The data is then returned as an object, with the title and description properties set accordingly.

The research property is an array of objects, with each object containing a title and content property. The content property has the '#' character replaced with '##' to create a subheading.

The vision, systemSpokesperson, collaboration, and possibilities properties are also included in the returned object.
